# Line endings.
#
# Every text blob in this repository is already stored with LF, and CI and both
# containers run on Linux. A Windows working tree that differs from them is how
# `rag-thesis-backend/services/retriever.py` ended up with 476 CRLF lines mixed
# into 255 LF ones: Pylint reported C0327 on every one of them and the score fell
# from 10.00 to 9.94, failing the local gate while CI stayed green and gave no
# hint why. Checking out LF everywhere means a local run reproduces CI exactly.
#
# After changing this file, normalize an existing clone once:
#     git add --renormalize .
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary. Never transformed, never diffed as text. `text=auto` would detect most
# of these anyway; declaring them is cheap insurance for the evidence artifacts
# and the paper, where a corrupting transform would be silent.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
